  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRA Joint Response Myanmar 2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;On October 27, 2023, Operation 1027 was launched, increasing widespread outbursts of violence. This resulted in the displacement of over 1 million individuals within Myanmar, adding to the already staggering number of IDPs. According to UNHCR, Rakhine (Central) and Magway are two of the hardest hit regions, with in total approximately 326.900 (Rakhine) and 239.700 (Magway) IDPs. In Rakhine, Ponnagyun township is hit hardest, receiving the highest number of new IDPs, with 52.084 new arrivals in the past few weeks, after the Arakan Army took over from the Myanmar Armed Forces (CCCM Cluster, May 2024). In Magway, Pakokku township is severely affected, with 31.699 new arrivals in the past period (FS Cluster, April 2024). In response to this escalation, ZOA and its local partners KYDO and CDDCET conducted a Rapid Needs Assessment (RNA) in these locations.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
